# Windows packaging must stay CRLF, in the repository and on every checkout.
#
# Not cosmetic. Notepad renders an LF-only file as one unbroken line, which is
# how a player would meet READ-ME-FIRST.txt; and cmd is documented to mis-parse
# a label that does not end CRLF, which would break install.bat in the one way
# that is hardest to diagnose. Without this, git's own eol handling strips the
# CRLF on checkout and the release built from that checkout ships broken files.
# tools/make-release.sh refuses to build if it ever finds them LF-only.
*.bat                              text eol=crlf
packaging/windows/READ-ME-FIRST.txt text eol=crlf

# Everything else is a Unix text file or a binary; leave git's defaults alone.
*.dll binary
*.gz  binary
